1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,650
Turn a client brief into a draft statement of work, a delivery backlog and
an audit report. Here the brief arrives by voice, and the words appear in
the message box while they are spoken.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:33,650
The audit runs before anything is published. When it fails, publishing is
blocked and the reason is shown. A repair pass lifts the score, and the new
version passes.

3
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:49,650
The approval is bound to this version, not to the run. The card states the
version, the mode, and exactly what will be created.

4
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:05,650
Every external call is journalled with a key that is stable across attempts,
so a retry cannot create a second epic.

5
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:19,650
In dry-run every call is validated and nothing is sent. That is the shipping
default, and the card says so.

6
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:43,650
Try the offline demo without API keys, or open the repository for the full
Docker setup. This is a draft for human review.
